        - Penpot audit: 19 visual component pages plus the source-blocked
          RadioButton page; every page has one named top-level board, Canvas
          Background #1b1b1b, font.baseGame at 12 px, linked palette colors,
          and no numeric CP437 stand-ins.

1.8 Component architecture rules:
    ☒ Organize the proposal into official DFHack widgets, custom generic components, DwarfSpec domain components, reusable screen panels, and workspace mockups.
    ☒ Give every component one clearly documented responsibility.
    ☒ Document what each complex component owns and explicitly does not own.
    ☒ Extract repeated structures instead of duplicating their shapes across components or mockup states.
    ☒ Compose official DFHack widgets and existing primitives inside domain components instead of copying their borders, labels, scrollbars, or interaction states.
    ☒ Keep cross-panel selection and synchronization in the workspace/controller layer rather than individual panels.
    ☒ Keep status calculation, aggregation, flake detection, sorting, capture, and editor launching outside presentation-only components.
    ☒ Avoid one component with a Cartesian product of unrelated variant dimensions.
    ☒ Prefer nested state components and content overrides over separate copies of an entire complex component.
    ☒ Do not create components for one-off headings, dividers, explanatory text, individual footer counts, stack separators, or complete workspace mockups.
    ☒ Create a component when an element is reused, has independent state or interaction, contains repeated children, owns scrolling or clipping, or appears across multiple mockup states.
        - Evidence: docs/test-runner-ui-foundation-contracts.md, "Component architecture".

1.9 Product and data ownership:
    ☒ Document the four selection levels: run, file or suite, test attempt, and command or event step.
    ☒ Define which selection level owns each action, status, summary, log, and evidence view.
    ☒ Define the minimum information required to answer: what failed, why, at which step, in which attempt, and what should be rerun.
    ☒ Define the boundary between the structured command trace and raw DFHack output.
    ☒ Define the boundary between DwarfSpec's Debug action and external VS Code debugging.
    ☒ Define a view-model contract for run state, progress, counts, scope, elapsed time, and reproduce command.
    ☒ Define a view-model contract for explorer nodes and their supplied aggregate statuses.
    ☒ Define a view-model contract for test results, attempts, failure category, behavior outcome, cleanup outcome, and infrastructure outcome.
    ☒ Define a view-model contract for trace steps, groups, durations, retry or wait data, source locations, evidence references, and raw-log anchors.
    ☒ Define a view-model contract for captured or textual host evidence and its availability state.
    ☒ Keep TEST RESULTS as the pane title; use the breadcrumb to identify its current scope.
    ☒ Show the selected test name and active attempt without overloading the breadcrumb.
        - Evidence: docs/test-runner-ui-foundation-contracts.md, "Product and data ownership".

1.10 Runtime capability decisions:
    ☒ Confirm which run modes can be configured.
    ☒ Confirm whether repeat count is configurable from the UI.
    ☒ Confirm whether the runner can report attempt-level outcomes.
    ☒ Confirm whether the runner can identify flaky outcomes within one repeated run.
    ☒ Confirm whether the runner can emit structured command and event steps.
    ☒ Confirm whether trace steps can identify source locations and raw-log anchors.
    ☒ Confirm whether the runner can provide retry, wait, or polling details.
    ☒ Confirm which host-evidence modes can be provided.
    ☒ Confirm whether evidence is live, captured, retained, inferred, or unavailable.
    ☒ Confirm whether Open Source can target file, line, and column in the configured editor.
    ☒ Confirm which debug-break and pause options are supported.
    ☒ Confirm whether Host Events can be separated reliably from raw DFHack output.
    ☒ Remove or mark unavailable every affordance not supported by the confirmed contracts.
        - Verified in Penpot: Open Source remains non-visible/unavailable;
          break/pause controls, raw-log-anchor claims, and retained-capture
          claims are absent; successful cleanup is silent.

