2.5 Generic components: Dropdown Field, Menu Panel, and Menu Item:
    ☒ Retain the existing closed and open Dropdown Control components.
    ☒ Document why Dropdown Control is required for a use case instead of CycleHotkeyLabel.
        - Dropdown is required when the complete option set must be visible to the
          user at selection time and the option count or label length makes cycling
          impractical. CycleHotkeyLabel is preferred for small, known finite sets.
    ☒ Extract or formalize the shared Dropdown Field used by both closed and open states.
    ☒ Keep the static label, selected value, and CP437 downward-triangle button inside Dropdown Field.
    ☒ Keep the triangle button free of surrounding brackets.
        - The existing Closed used a TextButton overlay (brackets visually hidden by
          BLACK fill). Dropdown Field uses a bare trigger area board with no TextButton.
    ☒ Show the triangle in the established normal color when closed and orange when open.
        - closed: 1px GREY stroke annotation on the CP437 031 board.
        - open: 1px LIGHTRED (#FF7111) stroke annotation on the CP437 031 board.
    ☒ Extract Dropdown Menu Panel with the same border treatment as Dropdown Field.
        - 280×94px, BLACK fill, 1px BROWN inner stroke.
    ☒ Extract Dropdown Menu Item for normal, focused, selected, and disabled states.
    ☒ Show a selected menu item with cyan text on a black background.
        - selected: COLOR_CYAN (#71BBB0) text on BLACK background.
    ☒ Refactor Dropdown Control Open to compose Dropdown Field, Dropdown Menu Panel, and repeated Dropdown Menu Item instances.
    ☒ Verify that refactoring the masters preserves all existing linked instances.
        - No external Open or Closed instances existed at refactor time.
    ☒ Create dedicated component pages for Dropdown Field, Dropdown Menu Panel, and Dropdown Menu Item.
        - Evidence: Penpot pages "Component - Dropdown Field" (State=closed/open
          variants; closed=GREY triangle, open=LIGHTRED triangle), "Component -
          Dropdown Menu Panel" (single component, BROWN border matching field),
          "Component - Dropdown Menu Item" (Presentation=normal/focused/selected/
          disabled; selected=CYAN text on BLACK). Dropdown Control Open refactored
          to compose linked Dropdown Field (open), Dropdown Menu Panel, and 4
          Dropdown Menu Item instances (options 1/2/4 normal, option 3 selected).

