Phase 3: Build the DwarfSpec domain component system
    ☒ Exit with linked DwarfSpec domain components that compose official and generic components without absorbing runner orchestration or runtime behavior.
        - Evidence: Penpot audit confirms all 12 dedicated domain-component
          pages for Attempt Indicator, Attempt Selector, trace rows, Command
          Trace, evidence values, Failure Comparison, Host Evidence, Failure
          Inspector, Run Summary, Reproduce Command, and Debug Options.

3.1 DwarfSpec component: Attempt Indicator:
    ☒ Create Attempt Indicator from an attempt number or label plus Status Indicator.
    ☒ Define normal, selected, focused, and disabled states without duplicating every possible status as parent-level artwork.
    ☒ Keep flake calculation outside Attempt Indicator.
    ☒ Create a dedicated component page for Attempt Indicator and its variants.
        - Evidence: Penpot "Component - Attempt Indicator" page. The linked
          Attempt Indicator component has one Interaction state axis with normal,
          selected, focused, and disabled variants. Each variant contains exactly
          one linked Status Indicator plus one supplied attempt-label slot; status
          selection and flake calculation remain outside the component. The page
          shows linked instances for every state in both specimen and reuse areas.

3.2 DwarfSpec component: Attempt Selector:
    ☒ Create Attempt Selector as a collection of Attempt Indicator instances plus current-attempt and total-attempt context.
    ☒ Evaluate ButtonGroup as the selection container before retaining the custom Attempt Selector layout.
    ☒ Retain the custom Attempt Selector only if ButtonGroup cannot represent per-attempt status and overflow requirements.
    ☒ Show a compact status for every supplied attempt.
    ☒ Define the no-repeat and single-attempt presentation without reserving dead space.
    ☒ Define overflow behavior for many attempts.
    ☒ Keep attempt selection outside the component's presentation contract.
        - Evidence: Penpot "Component - Attempt Selector" page. Attempt Selector
          has no-repeat, single-attempt, and many-attempts presentations. It
          composes linked Attempt Indicator instances with supplied current/total
          context. ButtonGroup was rejected because the only available master is
          incomplete and cannot express per-attempt status or horizontal overflow.
          The many-attempts strip clips horizontally while retaining nine linked
          supplied attempts, each with a linked Status Indicator; selection remains
          supplied from outside the component.
    ☒ Keep FLAKY defined by supplied inconsistent attempt outcomes unless historical data is explicitly available.
    ☒ Create a dedicated component page for Attempt Selector and its states.

3.3 DwarfSpec components: Trace Step Row and Trace Group Row:
    ☒ Define the ordered step taxonomy for setup, test commands, inputs, waits, assertions, cleanup, host events, and runner events.
    ☒ Create Trace Step Row from Status Indicator, optional Source Reference, and supplied step content.
    ☒ Show sequence, category, command or event, important target or argument, duration, and optional retry or wait information.
    ☒ Define queued, running, passed, failed, errored, skipped, cancelled, and not-run step states.
    ☒ Define selected, focused, expanded, and collapsed structural states without duplicating status artwork.
    ☒ Show retry, poll, or wait information only when supplied by the runner.
    ☒ Show a source reference only when one exists.
    ☒ Create Trace Group Row for setup, behavior, and cleanup grouping.
    ☒ Compose Status Indicator and existing CP437 expander assets in Trace Group Row.
    ☒ Show aggregate group status, duration, and child count.
    ☒ Keep group expansion from changing chronological ordering.
    ☒ Keep status aggregation outside Trace Group Row.
    ☒ Create dedicated component pages for Trace Step Row and Trace Group Row.
        - Evidence: Penpot "Component - Trace Step Row" and "Component - Trace
          Group Row" pages. Trace Step Row has normal, selected, focused,
          expanded, and collapsed structural variants, each with one linked Status
          Indicator; its status-input specimens cover queued, running, passed,
          failed, errored, skipped, cancelled, and not-run. Only the expanded
          presentation shows supplied poll/wait text and a linked Source Reference.
          Trace Group Row has setup, behavior, and cleanup variants, each composing
          linked Status Indicator and cp437.016 expander instances with supplied
          child-count and duration slots. Both pages state supplied-only aggregation
          and preserve setup-to-behavior-to-cleanup chronology.

3.4 DwarfSpec component: Command Trace:
    ☒ Create Command Trace from widgets.List, Trace Group Row, Trace Step Row, and the normal Scrollbar.
