3.6 DwarfSpec component: Host Evidence:
    ☒ Determine whether the runner can supply live rendering, captured frames, component-tree snapshots, or only textual state.
    ☒ Document supported evidence modes and their availability conditions.
    ☒ Create Host Evidence from Panel, an evidence viewport, Property List, Status Badge, TooltipLabel where contextual help is required, and supported overlay treatments.
    ☒ Show the evidence supplied for the selected trace step.
    ☒ When supplied, show focus path, active viewscreen, pointer position, input target, mounted-screen ownership, and selected widget bounds.
    ☒ Define unavailable, pending, stale, capture-failed, and host-disconnected states.
    ☒ Never label inferred state as captured or visually verified evidence.
    ☒ Do not make Host Evidence capture, infer, or retain runtime state.
    ☒ Do not imply full time travel unless the runner retains the required per-step state.
    ☒ Create a dedicated component page for Host Evidence and its states.
        - Capability decision: the runner can supply a bounded screen-cell capture
          when capture is invoked, a bounded component-tree snapshot, and textual
          focus/viewscreen context. It does not supply a retained live-render stream
          or per-step visual history; missing instrumentation remains unavailable.
        - Evidence: Penpot "Component - Host Evidence" page. Host Evidence has
          captured-current, unavailable, pending, stale, capture-failed, and
          host-disconnected states. Captured-current composes linked widgets.Panel,
          Status Badge, Property List, and widgets.TooltipLabel with a supplied
          screen-cell viewport, selected-widget-bounds overlay, and supplied focus,
          screen, pointer, target, mount, bounds, and tree metadata. All other
          states explicitly avoid inferred or retained visual evidence.

