Phase 6: Validate and hand off the proposal
    ☐ Exit only after conformance, component-linkage, viewer-flow, and unsupported-capability audits pass and the proposal is ready for product review.

6.1 Visual and component conformance:
    ☐ Keep all UI text at the single established game text size.
    ☐ Apply font.baseGame to every text shape.
    ☐ Link every text, fill, stroke, border, selection, and status color to an established DF palette preset.
    ☐ Use no unlinked solid color.
    ☐ Use existing CP437 tile assets for every visual symbol.
    ☐ Use the normal Scrollbar; do not introduce custom scrollbars.
    ☐ Use component-linked Divider instances; do not introduce one-off separator rectangles.
    ☐ Keep action buttons compact and free of dead space.
    ☐ Keep status indicators color-coded and understandable without color.
    ☐ Keep Tree View With Columns headerless with integrated row columns.
    ☐ Keep Generic Table View headers within the black, white, and brown palette.
    ☐ Keep Dropdown Menu Panel bordered like Dropdown Field.
    ☐ Keep selected dropdown items cyan on black.
    ☐ Keep the open dropdown triangle orange.
    ☐ Keep successful cleanup non-visible.
    ☐ Keep the host-responsive badge at the bottom-right.

6.2 Component verification:
    ☐ Verify that every custom component was evaluated against the official gui.widgets inventory.
    ☐ Verify that every retained custom control records why no official widget is appropriate.
    ☐ Verify that every extracted generic component has at least two demonstrated reuse points or an independent interaction responsibility.
    ☐ Verify that no generic component contains DwarfSpec-specific labels or rules.
    ☐ Verify that no domain component duplicates an existing DFHack control.
    ☐ Verify that every domain component composes linked official, generic, or existing component instances.
    ☐ Verify that every screen panel composes linked official, domain, and generic component instances.
    ☐ Verify that every workspace state composes linked screen-panel instances.
    ☐ Verify that changing a shared component master updates all intended dependent instances.
    ☐ Verify that master visibility changes do not hide linked instances.
    ☐ Verify that overrides do not detach instances unnecessarily.
    ☐ Verify that component names communicate responsibility rather than mockup position.
    ☐ Verify that no component owns both raw-log rendering and structured-trace rendering.
    ☐ Verify that no component owns both evidence capture and evidence presentation.
    ☐ Verify that no component owns both source presentation and editor launching.
    ☐ Verify that no component owns both status presentation and aggregate-status calculation.

6.3 Review and handoff:
    ☐ Review the primary flow as a Cypress-like run viewer rather than an IDE replacement.
    ☐ Verify that the command trace is more prominent than debug configuration.
    ☐ Verify that the selected test, attempt, and step are always unambiguous.
    ☐ Verify that behavior, infrastructure, cleanup, and host-health results cannot mask one another.
    ☐ Verify that the component dependency direction is: official DFHack widgets -> custom generic components -> DwarfSpec domain components -> screen panels -> workspace mockups.
    ☐ Audit the official 28-widget coverage matrix and confirm that all 20 previously missing standalone mockups are represented or explicitly deferred.
    ☐ Audit all visible text for the single game size and font.baseGame.
    ☐ Audit all fills and strokes for linked DF palette presets.
    ☐ Audit all visual symbols for existing CP437 asset usage.
    ☐ Audit all controls for reuse of existing DFHack widget components.
    ☐ Audit every page for the established dark Canvas Background.
    ☐ Audit every specimen for a clear top-level name.
    ☐ Audit Foundations for variants that belong on dedicated pages.
    ☐ Audit the final mockups for hidden obsolete layers and duplicate indicators.
    ☐ Exercise every prototype interaction from idle through failure triage and rerun.
    ☐ Record unresolved runtime dependencies and remove unsupported affordances from the final proposal.
    ☐ Obtain final product review of the revised Penpot proposal.
